---
const pips = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4];
const active = 2;
const options = ['12 seats', '10 seats', '8 seats'];
---

<div class="wrapper">
  <div class="sheet" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="panel">
      <header>
        <span class="eyebrow">CatalogObjectThumbnailOverlay.vue · HoverSelect.vue</span>
        <strong>Two controls, one for the styles and one for each axis</strong>
      </header>

      <div class="body">
        <figure class="part">
          <div class="carousel">
            <span class="counter"><span>3</span><span class="bar"></span><span>7</span></span>
            <button class="arrow prev" type="button" tabindex="-1">‹</button>
            <span class="silhouette"></span>
            <button class="arrow next" type="button" tabindex="-1">›</button>
            <ul class="pips">
              {pips.map((pip) => <li class:list={{ on: pip === active }}></li>)}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Group picker</strong>
            <p class="note">
              The thumbnail turns into a carousel when a cell holds more than one style. Arrows
              and pips step through them, the badge counts where you are, and the thumbnail
              slides so you can see which way you moved.
            </p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <figure class="part">
          <div class="select">
            <span class="current">10 seats <span class="caret">▾</span></span>
            <ul>
              {options.map((option, index) => (
                <li class:list={{ hovered: index === 0 }}>{option}</li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <figcaption>
            <strong>Axis dropdown</strong>
            <p class="note">
              Hovering an option shows that object in the thumbnail without committing to it.
              Moving the pointer off the list puts the old one back. A click is what picks.
            </p>
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <dl class="rules">
        <div>
          <dt>Window</dt>
          <dd>At most five pips. Past that the strip slides under a fixed middle pip</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Preview</dt>
          <dd><code>option-hover</code> changes the thumbnail, <code>option-click</code> changes the object</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>One control</dt>
          <dd>An axis with a single value loses its dropdown and keeps only the reading</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style lang="scss">
@use './sheet' as *;

@include sheet-chrome(46em);

.body {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
  gap: 1em;
}

.part {
  margin: 0;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 0.75em;
  align-items: start;
}

figcaption {
  display: grid;
  gap: 0.25em;

  strong {
    font-size: 0.75em;
  }
}

.carousel {
  position: relative;
  width: 8em;
  height: 5.5em;
  border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
  border-radius: 0.375em;
  background: linear-gradient(59deg, var(--surface-sunken) 0, var(--line) 100%);
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
}

.silhouette {
  width: 3.5em;
  height: 1.75em;
  border: 1.5px solid var(--ink-muted);
  border-radius: 100%;
  box-shadow:
    0 -0.5em 0 -0.4em var(--ink-muted),
    0 0.5em 0 -0.4em var(--ink-muted);
}

.counter {
  position: absolute;
  top: 0.375em;
  right: 0.375em;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 0.3ch;
  padding: 0.125em 0.375em;
  border: 1px solid var(--accent);
  border-radius: 0.75em;
  background: var(--surface-raised);
  font-size: 0.625em;

  .bar {
    width: 1px;
    height: 0.875em;
    rotate: 10deg;
    background: var(--ink-muted);
  }
}

.arrow {
  position: absolute;
  top: 50%;
  translate: 0 -50%;
  width: 1.5em;
  height: 1.5em;
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  padding: 0;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 0.25em;
  background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ink) 25%, transparent);
  color: var(--surface-raised);
  font-size: 0.75em;
  line-height: 1;

  &.prev {
    left: 0.25em;
  }

  &.next {
    right: 0.25em;
  }
}

.pips {
  position: absolute;
  bottom: 0.25em;
  left: 50%;
  translate: -50% 0;
  display: flex;
  gap: 0.25em;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;

  li {
    width: 0.5em;
    height: 0.5em;
    border: 1.5px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 100%;

    &.on {
      background: var(--accent);
    }
  }
}

.select {
  width: 8em;
  display: grid;
  font-size: 0.6875em;

  .current {
    position: relative;
    padding: 0.125em 0.5em;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0.25em 0.25em 0 0;
    background: var(--surface-sunken);
    text-align: center;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .caret {
    position: absolute;
    right: 0.5em;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--line-strong);
    border-top: none;
    border-radius: 0 0 0.25em 0.25em;
    background: var(--surface-sunken);
    text-align: center;

    li {
      padding: 0.125em 0.5em;

      & + li {
        border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      }

      &.hovered {
        background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 22%, transparent);
      }
    }
  }
}
</style>
